  "notes": [
    "-IR verb with an e→i stem change, following the same pattern as *vestir*. The stem change appears in the presente (all but nosotros/nosotras), the 3rd-person forms of pretérito indefinido (desvistió, desvistieron), and throughout the subjuntivo presente — including nosotros/nosotras (desvistamos), since e→i type -IR stem-changers keep the change in that form.",
    "Past participle is regular: **desvestido**.",
    "Not reflexive: *desvestir* means to undress someone or something else (a child, a patient, a doll). The reflexive form *desvestirse* (\"to undress oneself\") already exists as a separate verb file.",
    "*La enfermera desvistió al paciente con cuidado.* (\"The nurse undressed the patient carefully.\")",
    "*La madre desviste al bebé para el baño.* (\"The mother undresses the baby for the bath.\")",
    "Related: *desvestirse* (reflexive, \"to undress oneself\"), *vestir* (antonym, \"to dress\" — same e→i pattern), *la ropa* (clothes)."
  ],
